        <p>The attercian3e at the Birkenhead Show was below that of former y .ars owing to the unpropitious weather which atte,iled it. This was greatly to be regrettei as the entrif s i the more important sections,both for quality and number 3, have never before been excelled at Birken- head. 'nil number of entries was as follows :—Sleep 62, cattle 110. horses 515, pigeons 963, pen try 559, dogs 244, cher.se 67, hurter and eggs 90. horticulture 450, hooey 79, stands 103. The cl,,sses for dairy cows and Channel Island cattle were, as is usual at this show, thoroughly reprrsentative Mrs. Cyril E. Greenall, Walton Hall, Warrington, beiFig one of the chief exhibi.ors in the last named section.</p>
        <p>The prizJ winuera included the following loc4l ex hibitors:—</p>
        <p>CATTLE.-Shorthorns (District).-Bull, calved in or before 1898 : 3, J A Brown, Tarporley. Bull, calved in 1399 : 1 F Miller ; 2. T Adamson, Lostoek. Bolton ; 3, F Bibby Cow. in milk, calved in or before 1397 : 3, G Cooke,Chester• Heifer, calved in 1899 : 2, J A Brown. Tarporley. Dairy Cows (Open).-Cow in milk, any 9.7 e : 1. J A Brown, Tar- porley ; 3, 0 R Ward, Great Warlord, near Mobberley. Channel Islands (open).-1, Mrs Cyril 11 Greenall Warrington ; 2, L G Gisborne, Allestree Hall. Derby; 3, Mrs Cyril E Greenall. Cow in milk, calved in or before 1837 1 and 2, .xtrs C B Greenall 3. Marquis of Anglesey, Anglesey. Heifer, calved in 1898 : 1, L,G Gisborne, Derb7 . 2, W G M Townley, Grange-over-iiands ; 3. Mrs C B Greenall. Heifer, ealv•cl in 1899: 1, WG M Townley, Grange-over-Sands; 2. E Smith, King's Norton; 3. Mrs 0 B Greenall. Honsge.-Brood mare. any age, with foal at foot : 1. A Minty re. Lynam. Filly, foalei in 1397 : 1, 0 R Ward, Great Warlord. gobberley ; 2. S 3 Rainglll, Ringway ; Altrincharn. Filly,folded in 1893 : 1, T Davies, Bebington ; 2, it Dodd, Tarporley ; 3 L Dodd, Malpas. Filly, foaled in 1899 : 1, The Earl Egerton of Tattoo. Gelding, foaled in or before 1896: 1, A M'lntyre. Lvmm ;2, Jackson Brothers. Middle liulton. Wigan; 3. P Davies. Warburton. Draught and Agricultural Horses (District). -Mare. entered or eligible for entry in the Stud Book, foaled in or before 1896 : 1 and 2. J W Kenwortby ;3, 1' J Dutton, Saltne . Filly, foaled in 1897: 2, '2 J Dutton, Saltney ; 3 It Jeffs, Helsby, Warring- ton. Filly or Gelding, foaled in 1898: 1 T Davies, Bebing- ton ;2, R Dodd, Tarporley •, 3, L Dodd. Bickerton. Malpas. Hunters (open,.-M tre or Gelding, to carry upwards of 14 stone : 3, Ernest Brassey, Stamford Bridge, Chest,r Hack- ney (open).-Foal 1, Austin C Carr. Cheater. Mare foaled in or before 1893 : I. A L Goodson, Knutsford; 2,Billington Bros; 3,3 Makeague,Newton-le-Willows. District. -Brood Mare.any age,with foal at foot; 2, James Storrar, jun, Saughall,Chester; 3, William Parker. Sutton, Chester. Flacks or Riding ,ones (open).-Mare or gelding, exceeding 15 hands : 1, A L Goodson, Knutsford. CHERSE.-(Competition eonfined to farmers) -Three Cheshire Cheese, each 50Ib. or over : 1 and 2, J Jones; 3 and 4. R Vu ton ; 5, W Blockley ; 6. W Dutton. Three Cheshire Cheese, each over 21b. and under 52,1 b : 1, S A Bonet' ;2. E Langley ;3, G Weston ; 4, S Evans ;5, Miss E Arden ; 6. I` G,eenway. Three Cheshire Chaese,any weight. belonging to a farmer who has not won a first prize at any of this society's shows since 1897, inclusive : 1, S }Mans ;2, B Langley ;3. S A Bonell ; 4. G Platt :5, Mrs eeacock. CHALLENGE BOWLS.-J W Kenworthy Shire Brood Mare Challenge Cup (value 59 c.ulneas) for district competition : A Mlntyre. Lymm, with bay Bounce. Joseph Hoult Cheese Challenge Bowl, for farmers' competition : Richard Dutton, Ellesmere. Subscribers' Cheese Challenge Bowl (value 10 guineas, for farmers) : Evan Langley, Tarpurley. W H Lever Butter Challenge Bowl (value 10 guineas), for farmers : Mrs E Frame, Bunbury, Tarporley.</p>
        <p>HORSES.—Shlres (open). Stallion, foaled in or before 1897: 1, 3 W Kenworthy, Kahan ; 2, Earl Egerton, of *liftmen. Tatton Park_ stallion foaled in 1898: 3, 'earl Egerton of Tatton. Stallion, foaled in 1899: 1. 3 W Kenworthy ; 2. J Lewis; 3 3 K Christopherson. Hooton. Draught and Agricultural Horses (District).—Brood Mare. 16 hands and over, any age, with foal at foot : 1, P Allen. Willaston Hall, Chester; 2, 9 Jones, Little Sutton ; 3. T J Dutton, Saltney. Brood Mare, under 16 hands, any 9ge, with foal at foot: 1, A M'lntyre. Lymm ; 2, B Gibbon, Lvmm. Gelding. foaled in or before 1893 : 2; P Davie, Warburton. Cheshire. Hackneys (open).—Stallion, foaled in or before 1896 : AC Carr. Chester. Stallion, foaled in 1897 : 3, J Make Ague, Newton-le-Willows. Harness Classes (open).—Tandem Teams : Mare or gelding, exceeding 15 hands : 2, A L Goodson, Knutsford.</p>
