        <p>CHERE'S NOTHING HALF SO SWEET IN LIP% as LOVb'S YOUNG DRHAM. So sang Tom Moore years ago, and everyone who has been fortunate enough to consummate a happy engagement by a suitable marriage will doubtless coraially endorse his statement. what could be pleasanter than to be the proud poessessor of a nice home, presided over by a loving winsome wife, whose sole desire is to made things comfortable for you and the little ones—when they arrive? Rspecially do you realise the charm when you know that thanks to your own industry and the economical methods of the aforesaid good lady the "nest egg" at the bank Is steadily augmenting. Agreeable home surroumdings, of course, tend to heighten the felicity whilst upholding the family dignity. Good furnishings, attistivally and substantially constructed an' tastefully arranged, not only give pleasure to all beholders but have an educational, an elevating influence upon the chit ren, creates in their susceptible minds the desire to possess a similarly furnished home some day, supplied by the same good old firm their areas patronised, makes them frugal and thrifty, so that when they reach manhood or sr/man- hood other good orders are given to PITTS'S, of LONDON- ROAD AND GAY:LILL/RN, who fulfil them in a satisfactory manner, as usual.</p>
        <p>PiTT:,'S CELEBRATED HOUSE 3 OF FURNI- TURii at 14, 224, 284. 384, 50, 75. 100. 200 up to 1.000 guinexe, Pptcially augmented in quantity and quality of articles, represent the highest standArd of excellence pro- curable. Th,y easily excel others. Full particulars and new ILLUSTRATHD FURNISHING GLAD&amp; containing 700 designs, post free. Cash prices only quJted ; deferred pay- ments arranged.</p>
        <p>PITTS'6 DINING-ROOM SUITES (Second-hand). Magnificent solid wainut Suite, in rich Oriental saddlebags. with velvet borders, divan couch, and elegant easy and small chairs, cost £3O, fir £l3 ; massive spoon back Sidle, very fine, heavy frames in real skins, cost £35, for £l5 ; grand solid Oak buile frames exceptionally he4vy and elaborateiy carved, very uncommon design, cost £4O, for £ 7; another similar, in walnut, £lB. Two hundred to select from.</p>
        <p>DITTS'S. SIDEBOARDS (Second-hand) --Handy 1 Sideboard in vialnut, latest fie.Agn, fitted with dr twers, cupboard, &amp;c.. cost £7, for £3 ss. subst,ntial solid 'yak Sideboar massive itnd bold cost £lO. for £5 ; very special, solid Oak sideboard. splendid oesiga and w,rkmauship, cost £2, f-r £7;. mar7ellou, Sbiebo trd very imposing design, cosi £2O, for £9; gra,,d walnut :Adeboard. cost £24, for £l2 Scores to select from, astounding value, up to £6O each ; well worth. aiming. Dining Tables, all sizes, makes, and woods, at exceptionally low prices.</p>
        <p>P DRAWING-ROOM StiTES (Second- I. hand) —Artistic Chippendale Suite, Oriental covering, cost:£l2. for £6 103 ; inlaid mahogany Suite, covered in silk, cost £l6, for £9 ; Lhippendale Suite. expensive choice silk covering, cost £2:4 for £lO 10s; exquisite inlaid rosewood Suite, of choice character, latest deslgn, beautifully covered in silk tapestry, cost £25, for £,4 ; elegsnt Louis XV, Suite, In dark Chippendale mahogany, beautifully covered, cost £35, tor £l9. Over a hundred suites ,o select from, at all prices up to £4O each.</p>
        <p>DITTo'S DRAWING-ROONI CABINETS (Second- hand).—lnlaid Rosewood French Cabinet, beautiful design, cost £23 for £8 16s ; exquisite inlaid Rosewood Cabinet, exceptionally choice design, would grace any draw- ing room, cost £3O, for £l5 Scores of others to select from up to £6O each. Overmantels in endless variety.</p>
        <p>PITTS'S BEDROOM FUR ti ITUP.E (Second. .L hand). -B1 gent Bedroom Suite, landscane pattern. carved panels and bevelled pl-tes cost £lB for £lO ; tasteful. Suite in walnut, finely designed wardrobe, with bevelled mirrors, everything complete, large sized stands and tables, pedestal, rail, chairs, cost £3O, for £l5 ; magnificent Suite of lull number of uticles, all large, of best workmanship and design. cost £4O. for £18; another similar, cost £5O, for £24. A hundred others, up to £')o each.</p>
        <p>PPITTo'S BEDS [TADS AND BED DlNG.—Largest and best selection, being clearei out at giving-away prices, Rare chance for cheap lines.</p>
        <p>PITM'S CARPETS AND FLOOR COVERINGS. —Grand Display. All British makes, choicest designs. many excaisive ; exquisitely blended colourings. Laid and fitted free of charge. -DIM'S PIANOS, CYCLES, BASSINETTES, .1. MAIL CARTS. Lamps, Chins. Glass, Barthenware, Magnificent selection. Astounding value. Inspection Invited.</p>
