        <p>language in Lower Bank-street on the Ist August and with committing a breach ot the peace by acting in a eisorderly manner in Ship-yard on the 30th July—The evidence dis- clos,d the fact that at midnight on the let hist Ylargaret was parading Bank-street, brandishing a bill hook and challe ,ging her sister-in-law to fight. She made use oi filthy language.—Eviclence was given by P.C.'s Corbett and Chritnes.—Detendant was imprisoned for a day on the first charge and was bound over to keep the peace in ties second case.</p>
        <p>OBSCENE LANGUAGE.—For indulging in this osajectionable practice, James Clare. 3, Ashton's-yard was fined 5s and costs and Bridget McCoy, 17, Lower ship-yard !who did not appear) was fined 19s and costs.—The officers who proved the eases wer, P,C.'s Clarke and Reddington- WEDNESDAY—Before Mr. I:fireball (in tke chair), Councillar Smethurst amd Mr. Ci,ddes. A VI3LENT WOMAN—DISGRAC,FUL CoNnucr IN THE CELLs.—A young warnan named Rebecca Riley, was charged with having boon drink and disorderly at Brid,te Foot at 11-45 the prov,ons Baxendale proved the case. —The Chief Cons a'aie read the Bridovved sergeant's report on the case, which stated that prisoner's conduct in the cells was simply outrageous during a great part of the night. She was singing and shouting at the top of her voice, thus kee2ing the other prisoners awake. Such was her lung power that she could be distinctly heard in the street.—Mr. Talbot informed the magistrates that the prisoner had been before the Court eight times. tier husband WAS serving at the front and she was in receipt of Is 7•1 a day from the Military Authorities, which she made bad use of.—A fine of 5s and costs was im- posed. "A BIRD OF PassaGE."—John Moynihn was charged with being drunk and disordery in Buttermarket-street at 9.20 the previous night.—The Chief Constable said the man was a stranger to the town, being a" 1-drd of passage. He was one of those who " toil not, neither do they spin." (Laughter.) —A floe of 5s and costs was inflicted.</p>
