        <p>MCCORQUODA.LE CHALLENGE CUP.—NEWTON-LE-WILLOWS V. LoNDON.—The Newton Works team having beaten Leeds in the first round for this cop. played Londoa on Monday at Newton, or at any rate should have played them. The Lon- don team put in an appearance, but the wretched state of the weather prevented the game from being played to a finish. Play was commenced. Newton going to the wickets first,but after 19 runs had been scored, Jupiter Ptuvius put in an innings, arid the match had to be abandoned: An adjourn- ment was made to the Legh Arms Hotel where the usual dinner following on these pleasant matches was provided.and despite t e dispiriting condition of the elements outside, the meal was thoroughly enjoyed, about 63 sitting down. The evening was spent in a convivial manner, all present enjoy- ing themselves. RARLESTOWN PRIMITIVES V. S. HELENS TEMPERANCE RECS.—Played at St. Helens on Saturday. Score : PRIMITIVES. T EMI ERA.NCE RECS. W Mullins b Ellison... 4 Rigby lbw b Broster H Banton b Smedley Austin b Ellison Taylor c Davies b Ellison 1 Smedley b Morse thompton b Ellison... .. 1 Crosegrove c Mullins b Broster c Stubbs b Rigby... 13 Morse ... Morse not out... 4l fa Puncheon not out 1 Wilcox b Ellison Morris nGt out . W Puncheon b Broster 3 T Barnes c Wilcox b Morse Extras 7 Extras 2 Total 124 Total</p>
